    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>chore: adaptations for nightly-2026-03-22 <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/pull/201\">nightly#201</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Please review this PR. At the next toolchain release this diff will land in 'master'.</p>",
        "id": 580969312,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774225157
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This contains our changes to <code>inferInstanceAs</code> in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12897\">lean#12897</a>.</p>",
        "id": 580969550,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774225326
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It contains a smallish number of <em>new</em> backwards compatibility options like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">backward</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wrap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>to turn off the new behaviour. We <em>think</em> these represent problems in Mathlib, rather than the new <code>inferInstanceAs</code>, but would like to hear people's thoughts later --- not as part of reviewing this PR.</p>",
        "id": 580969858,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774225494
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As usual, there is a fair bit of churn around <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</code>, so I recommend asking your AI to mark files only containing such changes as viewed (or use this <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/kim-em/eb7208e1376177f676aaa488c0210dab\">script</a>).</p>",
        "id": 580970027,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774225591
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">bash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">curl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">fsSL</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">gist</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">githubusercontent</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">com</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">kim</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">em</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">eb7208e1376177f676aaa488c0210dab</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mark</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">option</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">viewed</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sh</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">leanprover</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">community</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">nightly</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">testing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">201</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580970681,
